		{"id":"0e663b93cddc1f5c","type":"text","text":"#### Weekly task (19/06/24):\n\n##### Convolutional neural network \n- Lecture 8: Deep learning software \n- Lecture 9: CNN architecture\n- Assignment 1\n\n##### Comp Arch\n- Turing complete - Level 33 (with notes)\n- Lecture 9: ISA and microarchitecture\n- Lecture 10: Microarchitecture Fundamentals and design\n##### Artificial Intelligence\n- Reinforcement learning - Cartpole problem\n- Reinforcement learning lecture 1\n- ~~Dynamic programming lecture~~ #school\n- Reinforcement learning lecture\n- ~~Revision of week 1-7 (17/06/24)~~ #school\n- ~~Revision of week 8-12 (18/06/24)~~ #school \n- ~~Practice exam~~ #school","x":-660,"y":-340,"width":720,"height":640,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"c42eda15f2dd262c","type":"text","text":"Turns out this week goals weren't achieve. I should follow the canvas guideline more and take this more seriously. It would seems like everything will be delayed. \nJune 26 week wasn't planned for goal either. \nI am learning how to be more disciplined. \nI do have to point out that I think this workload is achievable, with good discipline.   ","x":80,"y":160,"width":540,"height":240,"color":"#ff0000"},
		{"id":"cadce1d9f35379cd","type":"text","text":"Some improvements identified: \n1. Keep in the progress (even not as much)\n2. Do not have two days consecutive not being persistent \n3. Sometimes pursuing dream won't be always as enjoying, it could be boring or difficult. If that occurs, just dive in and keep on doing (not to track the progress or discourage from the delay)\n4. Having reflection is better - it allows me to face my improvements. Hence having a weekly reflection will be first thing I will be keep on doing from now. ","x":-80,"y":480,"width":580,"height":300}
